Z||000008||1FST2M6||06-28-2001||05:28 PM||||LOL.. not engineering.. Engineered... the shop i work with, Engineered Performance Inc. well i guess we do engineer stuff... well i've got nearly 4 years of an ME degree under my belt, the owner and the dyno tuner both have degrees from Ga. Tech.. so i'm sure theres not much we can't figure out..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but the shops claim to fame is custom turbo, superchargers, nitrous and N/A tuning. pulling 154hp out of my 2.8 auto is quite a feat... and now on the squeeze making 279hp at the wheels.. if they can my my car fast they can make ANYTHING fast. Shelby series 1, Ferraris, Alfas (sedans NOT graduates) and counless civics, supras, camaros etc are on the usual things to see at the shop at any given time. <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  <A HREF="http://www.epdyno.com" TARGET=_blank>www.epdyno.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.enthuza.com" TARGET=_blank>www.enthuza.com</A>  all the same shop... the dual exhaust on the miata will be on the 350hp miata the owner is reassembleing after it just got a shiney new yellow/pearl paint job... hope to see ya there! ||||reg||1
